.TH ZERODDS-WS-BRIDGED 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-ws-bridged \- DDS to WebSocket bridge daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-ws-bridged
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-listen\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-\-domain\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-topic\fR \fINAME\fR]...
[\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
[\fB\-\-metrics\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-ws-bridged
exposes selected DDS topics to WebSocket clients and forwards inbound WS
messages onto matching DDS publishers. It is the reference DDS \(<-) WS
bridge for the ZeroDDS distribution and implements
.IR docs/specs/zerodds-ws-bridge-1.0.md .
.PP
The daemon reads the YAML file given with
.BR \-\-config ,
with drop-ins in its sibling
.IR FILE .d/;
without that option it reads the system file
.I /etc/zerodds/ws-bridged.yaml
with
.I /etc/zerodds/ws-bridged.d/
(on macOS under
.IR /usr/local/etc/zerodds )
when it exists, and the built-in defaults otherwise.
On Linux it integrates with
.BR systemd (1)
via Type=notify; on macOS with
.BR launchd (8);
on Windows it runs as service
.BR ZeroDDSWSBridge .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
Path to the YAML configuration. See
.BR zerodds-ws-bridged.yaml (5).
.TP
.BR \-\-listen =\fIADDR\fR
Bind address. Default:
.IR 0.0.0.0:8080 .
.TP
.BR \-\-domain =\fIID\fR
DDS domain id. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-\-topic =\fINAME\fR
Single-topic override (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-cert =\fIFILE\fR
TLS cert (PEM); enables
.IR wss:// .
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-key =\fIFILE\fR
TLS key (PEM).
.TP
.BR \-\-auth\-token =\fISECRET\fR
Bearer token auth.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level =\fILEVEL\fR
Override the configured log level. One of
.IR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error .
Default:
.IR info .
.TP
.BR \-\-metrics =\fIADDR\fR
Prometheus scrape endpoint.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Version info.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print full option synopsis.
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable
file, syntax error or include cycle.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown (drain in-flight WS frames, unregister DDS readers).
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reads the configuration again: the TLS certificate and key files at their
configured paths, the auth settings and the topic ACL apply from then on
(the certificate to new connections). Changed TLS file paths, topics,
listen address or domain need a restart and are logged. A configuration
that does not load changes nothing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
Optional OTLP endpoint, such as http://localhost:4318.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal shutdown (SIGTERM/SIGINT).
.TP
.B 1
Configuration error.
.TP
.B 2
Bind error \(em address in use.
.TP
.B 3
DDS discovery error.
.TP
.B 4
TLS error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/zerodds/ws-bridged.yaml
Suggested deployment path, loaded only when selected with
.BR \-\-config .
Documented in
.BR zerodds-ws-bridged.yaml (5).
.TP
.I /var/log/zerodds/ws-bridged.log
Log target when
.I logging.destination
is
.IR file:... .
.TP
.I /var/lib/zerodds/
Persistent state (route shadows, durable WS session ids).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-ws-bridged.yaml (5),
.BR zerodds-mqtt-bridged (1),
.BR zerodds-admin (1),
.BR systemd.service (5).
.SH STANDARDS
DDS 1.4, RTPS 2.5, XTypes 1.3, RFC 6455 (WebSocket), RFC 7692 (permessage-deflate).
